/-!
# The Cohen structure theorem

Let `(R, 𝔪)` be a complete local ring with residue field `κ = R/𝔪`. This file proves that `R`
has a coefficient ring, and that when `𝔪` is finitely generated `R` is a quotient of a power
series ring in finitely many variables over a field or over a Cohen ring.

The whole argument runs through one construction: a ring map `Λ → R` out of a field or a Cohen
ring which carries nonunits into `𝔪` and whose composite with `R → κ` is surjective. Such a map
is built by successive lifting. Because `R` is `𝔪`-adically complete it is the inverse limit of
the `R/𝔪ⁿ`, so a ring map `Λ → R` is exactly a compatible system of ring maps `Λ → R/𝔪ⁿ`; and
a map `Λ → R/𝔪ⁿ` extends to `Λ → R/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹` whenever `Λ` is formally smooth over a base over which
both quotients are algebras, since `R/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹ → R/𝔪ⁿ` is surjective with square-zero kernel for
`n ≥ 1`. In residue characteristic zero one takes `Λ = κ`, which is formally smooth over `𝐙`
because `κ/𝐐` is separable and `𝐐` is a localization of `𝐙`. In residue characteristic `p > 0`
one takes for `Λ` a Cohen ring with residue field `κ` and lifts through the formally smooth maps
`𝐙/pⁿ𝐙 → Λ/pⁿΛ`. The coefficient ring of `R` is then the image of `Λ`, and the power series
presentation sends the variables to a finite generating set of `𝔪`.

## Main results

* `IsLocalRing.exists_isCoefficientRing_and_exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries`: the proof of
  [StacksProject 032A].

## Implementation notes

The inverse limit description of a complete ring is isolated as
`existsUnique_forall_quotient_mk_eq`: a compatible family of classes in the `R/Iⁿ` has a unique
common representative in `R`. Together with `exists_ringHom_of_compatible` and the recursion of
`exists_ringHom_of_liftStep` this reduces the construction of `Λ → R` to a single lifting step,
and `isNilpotent_ker_quotientFactor` supplies the square-zero kernel that step needs. The
statement of the lifting step is phrased over the fixed base `𝐙` in
`exists_ringHom_of_formallySmooth_int`, which is what the residue characteristic zero case uses;
the positive characteristic case needs a base varying with `n`, namely `𝐙/pⁿ𝐙`.

The two conclusions of the theorem are extracted from the same intermediate datum, recorded as
`HasCoefficientRingHom`, by `exists_isCoefficientRing_of_hasCoefficientRingHom` and
`exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries_of_hasCoefficientRingHom`; the second is the specialization of
Lemma 0315 that the source's proof appeals to.

The coefficient ring itself is the image of `Λ → R`, a quotient `Λ/J` of `Λ` by an ideal
contained in the maximal ideal. Its completeness is where the two cases of the source's proof
recombine: `J` is either zero, and then the image is isomorphic to `Λ` and adic completeness
transports along the isomorphism (`isAdicComplete_map_of_bijective`), or `Λ` is not a field,
hence a Cohen ring, and `J = 𝔪_Λ^k` for some `k` because the ideals of a discrete valuation ring
are the powers of its maximal ideal, so the maximal ideal of the image is nilpotent and adic
completeness is automatic (`IsAdicComplete.of_isNilpotent`). The remaining three conditions of
Definition 0326 come from the two properties recorded in `HasCoefficientRingHom`: that nonunits
of `Λ` map into `𝔪` makes the inclusion of the image local and identifies the contraction of
`𝔪` with the ideal generated by the residue characteristic, and surjectivity of `Λ → κ` makes the
map of residue fields surjective.

## References

* [StacksProject 032A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/032A), Theorem 10.160.8
* [StacksProject 0315](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0315), Lemma 10.96.1
-/

namespace Stacks.CompleteLocalRing.CohenStructure

open IsLocalRing

/-! ### A complete ring is the inverse limit of its adic quotients -/

/-- If `R` is `I`-adically complete then a family of classes `c n : R ⧸ Iⁿ` compatible with the
projections has a unique common representative in `R`; that is, `R = lim_n R/Iⁿ`. -/
private theorem existsUnique_forall_quotient_mk_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R)
    [IsAdicComplete I R] (c : ∀ n : ℕ, R ⧸ I ^ n)
    (hc : ∀ n, Ideal.Quotient.factor (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.le_succ n)) (c (n + 1)) = c n) :
    ∃! y : R, ∀ n, Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) y = c n := by
  classical
  have hmono : ∀ m n : ℕ, (h : m ≤ n) →
      Ideal.Quotient.factor (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (I := I) h) (c n) = c m := by
    intro m n h
    induction n, h using Nat.le_induction with
    | base => simp
    | succ n hmn ih =>
        obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (I := I ^ (n + 1)) (c (n + 1))
        rw [← ih, ← hc n, ← hz]
        simp [Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk]
  choose r hr using fun n : ℕ => Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (I := I ^ n) (c n)
  have key : ∀ {m n : ℕ}, m ≤ n → r m - r n ∈ I ^ m := by
    intro m n h
    refine Ideal.Quotient.eq.1 ?_
    rw [hr m, ← hmono m n h, ← hr n, Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk]
  obtain ⟨L, hL⟩ := IsPrecomplete.prec (I := I) inferInstance
    (f := r) (fun {m n} h => by rw [SModEq.sub_mem]; simpa using key h)
  have hLn : ∀ n, Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) L = c n := by
    intro n
    have h1 := hL n
    rw [SModEq.sub_mem] at h1
    have h2 : r n - L ∈ I ^ n := by simpa using h1
    rw [← hr n]
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq.2 (by simpa [neg_sub] using (I ^ n).neg_mem h2)
  refine ⟨L, hLn, ?_⟩
  intro y hy
  have hz : y - L = 0 := by
    refine IsHausdorff.haus (I := I) inferInstance _ (fun n => ?_)
    rw [SModEq.sub_mem]
    have h2 : Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) y = Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) L := by rw [hy n, hLn n]
    simpa using Ideal.Quotient.eq.1 h2
  linear_combination hz

/-- A compatible system of ring maps `Λ → R ⧸ Iⁿ` into the adic quotients of an `I`-adically
complete ring `R` comes from a ring map `Λ → R`. -/
private theorem exists_ringHom_of_compatible {Λ R : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R)
    [IsAdicComplete I R] (φ : ∀ n : ℕ, Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ n)
    (hφ : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : Λ),
      Ideal.Quotient.factor (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.le_succ n)) (φ (n + 1) x) = φ n x) :
    ∃ f : Λ →+* R, ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : Λ), Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) (f x) = φ n x := by
  classical
  choose g hg hg' using fun x : Λ =>
    existsUnique_forall_quotient_mk_eq I (fun n => φ n x) (fun n => hφ n x)
  refine ⟨{ toFun := g
            map_one' := (hg' 1 1 (fun n => by simp)).symm
            map_mul' := fun x y => (hg' (x * y) (g x * g y)
              (fun n => by simp [hg x n, hg y n])).symm
            map_zero' := (hg' 0 0 (fun n => by simp)).symm
            map_add' := fun x y => (hg' (x + y) (g x + g y)
              (fun n => by simp [hg x n, hg y n])).symm }, fun n x => hg x n⟩

/-- A compatible system of ring maps `Λ → R ⧸ Iⁿ` into the adic quotients of an `I`-adically
complete ring `R` comes from a ring map `Λ → R`. -/
alias exists_ringHom_of_compatible' := exists_ringHom_of_compatible

/-- A ring map into `R ⧸ I` which can be lifted one adic step at a time lifts to `R` itself,
provided `R` is `I`-adically complete. -/
private theorem exists_ringHom_of_liftStep {Λ R : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [CommRing R]
    (I : Ideal R) [IsAdicComplete I R] (P : ∀ n : ℕ, (Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ n) → Prop)
    (ψ : Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ 1) (hψ : P 1 ψ)
    (hlift : ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → ∀ g : Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ n, P n g →
        ∃ g' : Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ (n + 1), P (n + 1) g' ∧
          ∀ x, Ideal.Quotient.factor (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.le_succ n)) (g' x) = g x) :
    ∃ f : Λ →+* R, ∀ x, Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ 1) (f x) = ψ x := by
  classical
  have hsub : Subsingleton (R ⧸ I ^ 0) := Ideal.Quotient.subsingleton_iff.2 (by simp)
  choose L hLP hL using fun (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (g : Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ n) (hg : P n g) =>
    hlift n hn g hg
  set ρ : ∀ n : ℕ, {g : Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ (n + 1) // P (n + 1) g} :=
    fun n => Nat.rec ⟨ψ, hψ⟩
      (fun k ih => ⟨L (k + 1) (by omega) ih.1 ih.2, hLP (k + 1) (by omega) ih.1 ih.2⟩) n with hρ
  set φ : ∀ n : ℕ, Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ n := fun n =>
    Nat.casesOn n
      ({ toFun := fun _ => 0, map_one' := Subsingleton.elim _ _,
         map_mul' := fun _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _, map_zero' := rfl,
         map_add' := fun _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _ } : Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ 0)
      (fun k => (ρ k).1) with hφdef
  have hcomp : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : Λ),
      Ideal.Quotient.factor (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.le_succ n)) (φ (n + 1) x) = φ n x := by
    intro n x
    cases n with
    | zero => exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
    | succ k => exact hL (k + 1) (by omega) (ρ k).1 (ρ k).2 x
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := exists_ringHom_of_compatible I φ hcomp
  exact ⟨f, fun x => hf 1 x⟩

/-- For `n ≥ 1` the kernel of `R ⧸ Iⁿ⁺¹ → R ⧸ Iⁿ` is square zero, hence nilpotent. -/
private theorem isNilpotent_ker_quotientFactor {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) {n : ℕ}
    (hn : 1 ≤ n) : IsNilpotent (RingHom.ker (Ideal.Quotient.factor
      (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (I := I) (Nat.le_succ n)))) := by
  refine ⟨2, le_antisymm ?_ bot_le⟩
  rw [pow_two, Ideal.mul_le]
  intro r hr s hs
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (I := I ^ (n + 1)) r
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (I := I ^ (n + 1)) s
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem] at hr hs
  have h1 : x * y ∈ I ^ (n + n) := by rw [pow_add]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul hr hs
  have hxy : x * y ∈ I ^ (n + 1) := Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (by omega) h1
  simp only [← map_mul]
  exact (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem).2 hxy

/-- If `Λ` is formally smooth over `𝐙` and `R` is `I`-adically complete, then every ring map
`Λ → R ⧸ I` lifts to a ring map `Λ → R`. -/
@[ega "0 19.3.11" "special case"]
private theorem exists_ringHom_of_formallySmooth_int {Λ R : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [CommRing R]
    (hΛ : Algebra.FormallySmooth ℤ Λ) (I : Ideal R) [IsAdicComplete I R] (ψ : Λ →+* R ⧸ I ^ 1) :
    ∃ f : Λ →+* R, ∀ x, Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ 1) (f x) = ψ x := by
  have := hΛ
  refine exists_ringHom_of_liftStep I (fun _ _ => True) ψ trivial (fun n hn g _ => ?_)
  refine Exists.imp (fun g' hg' => ⟨trivial, hg'⟩) ?_
  set π : (R ⧸ I ^ (n + 1)) →ₐ[ℤ] R ⧸ I ^ n :=
    (Ideal.Quotient.factor (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (I := I) (Nat.le_succ n))).toIntAlgHom with hπ
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective π :=
    Ideal.Quotient.factor_surjective (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (I := I) (Nat.le_succ n))
  have hnil : IsNilpotent (RingHom.ker (π : (R ⧸ I ^ (n + 1)) →+* R ⧸ I ^ n)) :=
    isNilpotent_ker_quotientFactor I hn
  exact ⟨(Algebra.FormallySmooth.liftOfSurjective g.toIntAlgHom π hsurj hnil).toRingHom,
    fun x => Algebra.FormallySmooth.liftOfSurjective_apply g.toIntAlgHom π hsurj hnil x⟩

/-- Adic completeness transports along a ring isomorphism. -/
private theorem isAdicComplete_map_of_bijective {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    (f : A →+* B) (hf : Function.Bijective f) (I : Ideal A) [IsAdicComplete I A] :
    IsAdicComplete (I.map f) B := by
  set e : A ≃+* B := RingEquiv.ofBijective f hf with he
  have hef : ∀ a : A, e a = f a := fun a => rfl
  have hmem : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : B), x ∈ (I.map f) ^ n ↔ e.symm x ∈ I ^ n := by
    intro n x
    rw [← Ideal.map_pow, Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective f hf.2]
    refine ⟨?_, fun h => ⟨e.symm x, h, by rw [← hef, e.apply_symm_apply]⟩⟩
    rintro ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    rwa [← hef, e.symm_apply_apply]
  rw [isAdicComplete_iff]
  constructor
  · refine ⟨fun x hx => ?_⟩
    have h0 : e.symm x = 0 := by
      refine IsHausdorff.haus (I := I) inferInstance _ (fun n => ?_)
      rw [SModEq.zero]
      have h := hx n
      rw [SModEq.zero] at h
      have h1 : x ∈ (I.map f) ^ n := by simpa using h
      simpa using (hmem n x).1 h1
    rw [← e.apply_symm_apply x, h0, map_zero]
  · refine ⟨fun {g} hg => ?_⟩
    have hcompat : ∀ {m n : ℕ}, m ≤ n → (fun k => e.symm (g k)) m ≡ (fun k => e.symm (g k)) n
        [SMOD I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A A)] := by
      intro m n hmn
      rw [SModEq.sub_mem]
      have h1 := hg hmn
      rw [SModEq.sub_mem] at h1
      have h2 : g m - g n ∈ (I.map f) ^ m := by simpa using h1
      have h3 := (hmem m _).1 h2
      rw [map_sub] at h3
      simpa using h3
    obtain ⟨L, hL⟩ := IsPrecomplete.prec (I := I) inferInstance hcompat
    refine ⟨e L, fun n => ?_⟩
    rw [SModEq.sub_mem]
    have h1 := hL n
    rw [SModEq.sub_mem] at h1
    have h2 : e.symm (g n) - L ∈ I ^ n := by simpa using h1
    have h3 : e.symm (g n - e L) ∈ I ^ n := by
      rwa [map_sub, e.symm_apply_apply]
    simpa using (hmem n (g n - e L)).2 h3

/-! ### The datum both halves of the theorem are assembled from -/

/-- The datum out of which both halves of the Cohen structure theorem are assembled: a ring `Λ`
which is a field or a Cohen ring, and is a Cohen ring whenever the residue characteristic of `R`
is positive, whose maximal ideal is generated by that residue characteristic, together with a ring
map `Λ → R` carrying nonunits of `Λ` into `𝔪` and surjective onto the residue field of `R`. -/
def HasCoefficientRingHom (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] : Prop :=
  ∃ (Λ : Type u) (_ : CommRing Λ) (_ : IsDomain Λ) (_ : IsLocalRing Λ),
    (IsField Λ ∨ IsCohenRing Λ) ∧
      (ringChar (ResidueField R) ≠ 0 → IsCohenRing Λ) ∧
      maximalIdeal Λ = Ideal.span {(ringChar (ResidueField R) : Λ)} ∧
        ∃ f : Λ →+* R, (∀ x : Λ, ¬ IsUnit x → f x ∈ maximalIdeal R) ∧
          Function.Surjective ((residue R).comp f)

/-- If `m ∈ J`, the quotient `A ⧸ J` is an algebra over `ZMod m`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
private noncomputable def zmodAlgebraQuotient {A : Type*} [CommRing A] (m : ℕ) (J : Ideal A)
    (h : (m : A) ∈ J) : Algebra (ZMod m) (A ⧸ J) :=
  have h0 : (m : A ⧸ J) = 0 := by
    rw [← map_natCast (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)]
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 h
  letI : CharP (A ⧸ J) (ringChar (A ⧸ J)) := ringChar.charP _
  (ZMod.castHom (ringChar.dvd h0) (A ⧸ J)).toAlgebra

/-- Every ring homomorphism between `ZMod m`-algebras is `ZMod m`-linear, the `ZMod m`-algebra
structure on a ring being unique (`RingHom.ext_zmod`). -/
private def zmodAlgHom {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (m : ℕ) [Algebra (ZMod m) A]
    [Algebra (ZMod m) B] (f : A →+* B) : A →ₐ[ZMod m] B :=
  { f with
    commutes' := fun r => DFunLike.congr_fun
      (RingHom.ext_zmod (f.comp (algebraMap (ZMod m) A)) (algebraMap (ZMod m) B)) r }

/-- A ring map `f : Λ → R` lifting `g : Λ → R/𝔪` through `R/𝔪¹` is a lift of `g` to `R`. -/
private theorem residue_eq_of_quotient_mk_eq {Λ R : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [CommRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] (f : Λ →+* R) (g : Λ →+* ResidueField R)
    (hf : ∀ x, Ideal.Quotient.mk (maximalIdeal R ^ 1) (f x) =
      (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (pow_one (maximalIdeal R))).symm (g x)) (x : Λ) :
    residue R (f x) = g x := by
  have h : Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (pow_one (maximalIdeal R))
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (maximalIdeal R ^ 1) (f x)) = g x := by
    rw [hf x]
    exact (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (pow_one (maximalIdeal R))).apply_symm_apply _
  rwa [Ideal.quotEquivOfEq_mk] at h

/-- A field `κ` of characteristic zero is formally smooth over `𝐙`: the extension `κ/𝐐` is
separable, hence formally smooth (Stacks 0322), `𝐐` is a localization of `𝐙` and therefore
formally smooth over it, and formal smoothness is stable under composition. -/
private theorem formallySmooth_int_of_charZero (κ : Type u) [Field κ] [CharZero κ] :
    Algebra.FormallySmooth ℤ κ := by
  obtain ⟨hsep, htfae⟩ := Algebra.isSeparableExtension_of_charZero_and_tfae ℚ κ
  have : Algebra.FormallySmooth ℚ κ := (htfae.out 1 6).mp (hsep inferInstance)
  have : Algebra.FormallySmooth ℤ ℚ :=
    Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_isLocalization (nonZeroDivisors ℤ)
  exact Algebra.FormallySmooth.comp ℤ ℚ κ

/-- In residue characteristic zero the residue field itself is a coefficient ring: it is formally
smooth over `𝐙`, because `κ/𝐐` is separable (Stacks 0322) and `𝐐` is a localization of `𝐙`, so
the identity of `κ` lifts through the tower of the `R/𝔪ⁿ` to a section `κ → R`. -/
@[ega "0 19.6.2" "special case"]
private theorem hasCoefficientRingHom_of_charZero (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R] [CharZero (ResidueField R)] :
    HasCoefficientRingHom R := by
  have hfs : Algebra.FormallySmooth ℤ (ResidueField R) := formallySmooth_int_of_charZero _
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := exists_ringHom_of_formallySmooth_int hfs (maximalIdeal R)
    (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (pow_one (maximalIdeal R))).symm.toRingHom
  have key : ∀ x : ResidueField R, residue R (f x) = x :=
    residue_eq_of_quotient_mk_eq f (RingHom.id _) hf
  refine ⟨ResidueField R, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    Or.inl (Field.toIsField _), ?_, ?_, f, fun x hx => ?_, fun y => ⟨y, key y⟩⟩
  · intro hc
    exact (hc (ringChar.eq_zero (R := ResidueField R))).elim
  · rw [ringChar.eq_zero (R := ResidueField R)]
    simpa using isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq.1 (Field.toIsField (ResidueField R))
  · rw [not_not.1 (fun hx0 : x ≠ 0 => hx (isUnit_iff_ne_zero.2 hx0)), map_zero]
    exact Submodule.zero_mem _

/-- In residue characteristic `p > 0` a Cohen ring `Λ` with residue field `κ` (Stacks 0328) is a
coefficient ring: the isomorphism `Λ/pΛ = κ` lifts through the tower of the `R/𝔪ⁿ` because every
`𝐙/pⁿ𝐙 → Λ/pⁿΛ` is formally smooth (Stacks 0329). -/
@[ega "0 19.8.6" "(ii), special case", sga "7 IX 12.8" "more general"]
private theorem hasCoefficientRingHom_of_charP (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R] (p : ℕ) (hp : p ≠ 0)
    [CharP (ResidueField R) p] : HasCoefficientRingHom R := by
  have hpp : p.Prime := (CharP.char_is_prime_or_zero (ResidueField R) p).resolve_right hp
  obtain ⟨Λ, _, _, _, hmax, ⟨e⟩⟩ :=
    IsCohenRing.exists_residueField_ringEquiv p hpp (ResidueField R)
  have hcharΛ : CharP (ResidueField Λ) p :=
    charP_of_injective_ringHom (f := e.symm.toRingHom) e.symm.injective p
  have hpR : (p : R) ∈ maximalIdeal R := by
    have h0 : (p : ResidueField R) = 0 := CharP.cast_eq_zero (ResidueField R) p
    rw [← map_natCast (residue R) p] at h0
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.1 h0
  set ψ : Λ →+* R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ 1 :=
    (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (pow_one (maximalIdeal R))).symm.toRingHom.comp
      (e.toRingHom.comp (residue Λ)) with hψdef
  have hψ : ψ ((p : Λ) ^ 1) = 0 := by
    have h0 : residue Λ ((p : Λ) ^ 1) = 0 := by
      refine Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 ?_
      rw [pow_one, hmax]
      exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
    have h1 : ψ ((p : Λ) ^ 1)
        = (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (pow_one (maximalIdeal R))).symm
          (e (residue Λ ((p : Λ) ^ 1))) := by rw [hψdef]; rfl
    rw [h1, h0, map_zero]
    exact map_zero _
  have main : ∃ f : Λ →+* R, ∀ x, Ideal.Quotient.mk (maximalIdeal R ^ 1) (f x) = ψ x := by
    refine exists_ringHom_of_liftStep (maximalIdeal R)
      (fun n g => g ((p : Λ) ^ n) = 0) ψ hψ ?_
    intro n hn g hg
    let _ : Algebra (ZMod (p ^ (n + 1))) (Λ ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : Λ) ^ (n + 1)}) :=
      zmodAlgebraQuotient _ _ (by rw [Nat.cast_pow]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
    let _ : Algebra (ZMod (p ^ (n + 1))) (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1)) :=
      zmodAlgebraQuotient _ _ (by rw [Nat.cast_pow]; exact Ideal.pow_mem_pow hpR _)
    let _ : Algebra (ZMod (p ^ (n + 1))) (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ n) :=
      zmodAlgebraQuotient _ _ (by
        rw [Nat.cast_pow]
        exact Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.le_succ n) (Ideal.pow_mem_pow hpR _))
    have hfs : Algebra.FormallySmooth (ZMod (p ^ (n + 1)))
        (Λ ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : Λ) ^ (n + 1)}) :=
      IsCohenRing.formallySmooth_quotient_span_pow p (n + 1) Λ
    have hker : ∀ a ∈ Ideal.span {(p : Λ) ^ (n + 1)}, g a = 0 := by
      intro a ha
      obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 ha
      rw [map_mul, pow_succ, map_mul, hg, zero_mul, mul_zero]
    set g₁ : (Λ ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : Λ) ^ (n + 1)}) →+* R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ n :=
      Ideal.Quotient.lift _ g hker with hg₁
    set π : (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ (n + 1)) →+* R ⧸ maximalIdeal R ^ n :=
      Ideal.Quotient.factor (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (I := maximalIdeal R) (Nat.le_succ n))
      with hπ
    have hsurj : Function.Surjective (zmodAlgHom (p ^ (n + 1)) π) :=
      Ideal.Quotient.factor_surjective
        (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (I := maximalIdeal R) (Nat.le_succ n))
    have hnil : IsNilpotent (RingHom.ker (zmodAlgHom (p ^ (n + 1)) π).toRingHom) :=
      isNilpotent_ker_quotientFactor (maximalIdeal R) hn
    have := hfs
    refine ⟨(Algebra.FormallySmooth.liftOfSurjective (zmodAlgHom (p ^ (n + 1)) g₁)
      (zmodAlgHom (p ^ (n + 1)) π) hsurj hnil).toRingHom.comp
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(p : Λ) ^ (n + 1)})), ?_, fun x => ?_⟩
    · have h0 : Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(p : Λ) ^ (n + 1)}) ((p : Λ) ^ (n + 1)) = 0 :=
        Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
      simp [h0]
    · have h1 := Algebra.FormallySmooth.liftOfSurjective_apply (zmodAlgHom (p ^ (n + 1)) g₁)
        (zmodAlgHom (p ^ (n + 1)) π) hsurj hnil (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x)
      simpa [hg₁, hπ, zmodAlgHom] using h1
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := main
  have key : ∀ x : Λ, residue R (f x) = e (residue Λ x) :=
    residue_eq_of_quotient_mk_eq f (e.toRingHom.comp (residue Λ)) hf
  refine ⟨Λ, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, Or.inr inferInstance,
    (fun _ => inferInstance), ?_, f,
    fun x hx => ?_, fun y => ?_⟩
  · rw [hmax, ringChar.eq (ResidueField R) p]
  · have hx' : residue Λ x = 0 :=
      Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 ((mem_maximalIdeal x).2 hx)
    have hkx := key x
    rw [hx', map_zero] at hkx
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.1 hkx
  · obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := e.surjective y
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (I := maximalIdeal Λ) z
    refine ⟨w, ?_⟩
    change residue R (f w) = y
    rw [key w, show residue Λ w = z from hw, hz]

/-- Every complete local ring carries the datum of `HasCoefficientRingHom`, by cases on the
characteristic of its residue field. -/
theorem hasCoefficientRingHom (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R] : HasCoefficientRingHom R := by
  rcases eq_or_ne (ringChar (ResidueField R)) 0 with hp | hp
  · have : CharP (ResidueField R) 0 := hp ▸ ringChar.charP (ResidueField R)
    have := CharP.charP_to_charZero (ResidueField R)
    exact hasCoefficientRingHom_of_charZero R
  · have hcp : CharP (ResidueField R) (ringChar (ResidueField R)) := ringChar.charP _
    exact hasCoefficientRingHom_of_charP R (ringChar (ResidueField R)) hp

/-- The image of a coefficient ring map is a coefficient ring of `R` (Stacks 0326): its maximal
ideal is the contraction of `𝔪` because the map carries nonunits to nonunits, it is complete
because it is either isomorphic to `Λ` or has nilpotent maximal ideal, and its residue field is
that of `R` by construction. -/
private theorem exists_isCoefficientRing_of_hasCoefficientRingHom (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] (h : HasCoefficientRingHom R) :
    ∃ Λ : LocalSubring R, Λ.IsCoefficientRing := by
  obtain ⟨Λ, _, _, _, hcase, -, hmax, f, hnu, hsurj⟩ := h
  set c : ℕ := ringChar (ResidueField R) with hc
  set S := f.range with hSdef
  set f' := f.rangeRestrict with hf'def
  have hf'surj : Function.Surjective f' := f.rangeRestrict_surjective
  have hunit : ∀ x : Λ, IsUnit (f x) → IsUnit x := by
    intro x hx
    by_contra hu
    exact (mem_maximalIdeal (f x)).1 (hnu x hu) hx
  have : IsLocalRing S := IsLocalRing.of_surjective' f' hf'surj
  have hlh : IsLocalHom S.subtype := by
    refine ⟨fun a ha => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hf'surj a
    exact (hunit x ha).map f'
  have hmemiff : ∀ x : Λ, f' x ∈ (maximalIdeal R).comap S.subtype ↔ x ∈ maximalIdeal Λ := by
    intro x
    simp only [Ideal.mem_comap, mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff]
    exact not_congr ⟨fun hu => hunit x hu, fun hu => hu.map f⟩
  have hspan : (maximalIdeal R).comap S.subtype = Ideal.span {(c : S)} := by
    refine le_antisymm (fun a ha => ?_) ?_
    · obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hf'surj a
      have hx := (hmemiff x).1 ha
      rw [hmax, Ideal.mem_span_singleton'] at hx
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hx
      refine Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.2 ⟨f' y, ?_⟩
      rw [← map_natCast f' c, ← map_mul, hy]
    · simp only [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.mem_coe]
      rw [← map_natCast f' c]
      exact (hmemiff _).2 (by rw [hmax]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
  have hmS : maximalIdeal S = Ideal.span {(c : S)} :=
    (maximalIdeal_comap S.subtype).symm.trans hspan
  have hACΛ : IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal Λ) Λ := by
    rcases hcase with hfld | hcoh
    · refine IsAdicComplete.of_isNilpotent _ ⟨1, ?_⟩
      rw [pow_one, Ideal.zero_eq_bot]
      exact isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq.1 hfld
    · have := hcoh; infer_instance
  have hACS : IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal S) S := by
    have hmapeq : maximalIdeal S = Ideal.map f' (maximalIdeal Λ) := by
      rw [hmS, hmax, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_natCast]
    have hkerle : RingHom.ker f' ≤ maximalIdeal Λ := by
      refine le_maximalIdeal fun htop => ?_
      have h1 : (1 : Λ) ∈ RingHom.ker f' := htop ▸ Submodule.mem_top
      rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_one] at h1
      exact one_ne_zero h1
    rw [hmapeq]
    rcases eq_or_ne (RingHom.ker f') ⊥ with hk | hk
    · exact isAdicComplete_map_of_bijective f'
        ⟨(RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot f').2 hk, hf'surj⟩ _
    · have hnf : ¬ IsField Λ := fun hfld =>
        hk (le_bot_iff.1 (hkerle.trans_eq (isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq.1 hfld)))
      have hcoh : IsCohenRing Λ := hcase.resolve_left hnf
      have hirr : Irreducible ((c : Λ)) :=
        (IsDiscreteValuationRing.irreducible_iff_uniformizer _).2 hmax
      obtain ⟨k, hkk⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.ideal_eq_span_pow_irreducible hk hirr
      have hle : maximalIdeal Λ ^ k ≤ RingHom.ker f' :=
        le_of_eq (by rw [hkk, hmax, Ideal.span_singleton_pow])
      refine IsAdicComplete.of_isNilpotent _ ⟨k, ?_⟩
      rw [Ideal.zero_eq_bot, ← Ideal.map_pow, Ideal.map_eq_bot_iff_le_ker]
      exact hle
  have hres : Function.Surjective (ResidueField.map S.subtype) := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hsurj y
    exact ⟨residue S (f' x), by rwa [ResidueField.map_residue]⟩
  refine ⟨LocalSubring.mk S, ?_⟩
  exact { isLocalHom := hlh
          isAdicComplete := hACS
          residueField_map_surjective := hres
          comap_maximalIdeal_eq_span_ringChar := hspan }

/-- Let `R` be `I`-adically complete, let `y_1, …, y_n` generate `I`, and let `f : Λ → R` be a
ring map which is surjective modulo `I`. Then evaluation at the `y_i`,
`Λ[[x_1, …, x_n]] → R`, `x_i ↦ y_i`, is a surjective ring map (Stacks 0315).

The map is `MvPowerSeries.eval₂Hom` for the `I`-adic topology on `R`, in which the `y_i` are
topologically nilpotent; surjectivity is `surjective_of_mk_map_comp_surjective`, both power
series ring and `R` being adically complete for the ideal generated by the variables and its
image `I`. -/
@[sga "1 II 4.14" "special case"]
theorem exists_surjective_eval₂Hom {Λ R : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [CommRing R]
    (I : Ideal R) [IsAdicComplete I R] {n : ℕ} (y : Fin n → R)
    (hy : Ideal.span (Set.range y) = I) (f : Λ →+* R)
    (hf : Function.Surjective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk I).comp f)) :
    ∃ F : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →+* R, Function.Surjective F ∧
      (∀ i, F (MvPowerSeries.X i) = y i) ∧ ∀ c : Λ, F (MvPowerSeries.C c) = f c := by
  let _ : WithIdeal Λ := ⟨⊥⟩
  have : DiscreteTopology Λ := is_bot_adic_iff.1 rfl
  let _ : WithIdeal R := ⟨I⟩
  obtain ⟨hcs, ht2⟩ := (IsAdic.isAdicComplete_iff (I := I) rfl).1 ‹IsAdicComplete I R›
  have := hcs
  have := ht2
  have hyI : ∀ i, y i ∈ I := fun i => hy ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
  have ha : MvPowerSeries.HasEval y :=
    { hpow := fun i => WithIdeal.isTopologicallyNilpotent_of_mem (hyI i)
      tendsto_zero := by simp [Filter.cofinite_eq_bot] }
  set F : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →+* R :=
    MvPowerSeries.eval₂Hom (φ := f) continuous_of_discreteTopology ha with hFdef
  have hFc : ⇑F = MvPowerSeries.eval₂ f y := MvPowerSeries.coe_eval₂Hom _ _
  have hFX : ∀ i, F (MvPowerSeries.X i) = y i := fun i => by
    rw [hFc]; exact MvPowerSeries.eval₂_X f y i
  have hFC : ∀ c : Λ, F (MvPowerSeries.C c) = f c := fun c => by
    rw [hFc]; exact MvPowerSeries.eval₂_C f y c
  have hmapF : Ideal.map F
      (Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X (σ := Fin n) (R := Λ)))) = I := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, ← hy, ← Set.range_comp]
    exact congrArg _ (congrArg Set.range (funext hFX))
  have hhaus : IsHausdorff (Ideal.map F
      (Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X (σ := Fin n) (R := Λ))))) R := by
    rw [hmapF]; infer_instance
  refine ⟨F, ?_, hFX, hFC⟩
  refine surjective_of_mk_map_comp_surjective (I := Ideal.span (Set.range
    (MvPowerSeries.X (σ := Fin n) (R := Λ)))) F fun b => ?_
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective b
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hf (Ideal.Quotient.mk I r)
  refine ⟨MvPowerSeries.C c, ?_⟩
  rw [RingHom.comp_apply, hFC c, ← hr]
  exact Ideal.Quotient.eq.2 (by rw [hmapF]; exact Ideal.Quotient.eq.1 hc)

/-- If `𝔪` is generated by `y_1, …, y_n` and `Λ → R` is a coefficient ring map, then
`Λ[[x_1, …, x_n]] → R`, `x_i ↦ y_i`, is surjective: it is surjective modulo `(x_1, …, x_n)` and
both sides are `(x_1, …, x_n)`-adically complete (Stacks 0315). -/
private theorem exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries_of_hasCoefficientRingHom (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R] (hFG : (maximalIdeal R).FG)
    (h : HasCoefficientRingHom R) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (Λ : Type u) (_ : CommRing Λ) (_ : IsDomain Λ),
      (IsField Λ ∨ IsCohenRing Λ) ∧
        ∃ f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →+* R, Function.Surjective f := by
  obtain ⟨Λ, _, _, _, hcase, -, -, f, -, hf⟩ := h
  obtain ⟨n, y, hy⟩ := Submodule.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family.1 hFG
  obtain ⟨F, hFsurj, -, -⟩ := exists_surjective_eval₂Hom (maximalIdeal R) y hy f hf
  exact ⟨n, Λ, inferInstance, inferInstance, hcase, F, hFsurj⟩

end Stacks.CompleteLocalRing.CohenStructure

/-!
# The Cohen structure theorem

Let `(R, 𝔪)` be a complete local ring, that is a local ring which is complete and separated for
its maximal-ideal-adic topology, so that `R → lim_n R/𝔪^n` is an isomorphism. The Cohen structure
theorem says two things about such an `R`.

First, `R` has a coefficient ring (Stacks 0326): a local subring `Λ ⊆ R` which is itself complete,
whose maximal ideal is `Λ ∩ 𝔪`, which maps isomorphically onto the residue field of `R`, and for
which `Λ ∩ 𝔪 = pΛ` with `p` the characteristic of that residue field. Such a `Λ` is a field when
`p = 0`, a Cohen ring (Stacks 0327) when `p > 0` and no power of `p` vanishes in `R`, and an
Artinian local ring with maximal ideal `(p)` otherwise. It is produced by lifting the identity of
the residue field successively through `R/𝔪ⁿ → R/𝔪ⁿ⁻¹`, which is possible because `κ/ℚ` is
formally smooth in the first case and `ℤ/pⁿℤ → Λ/pⁿΛ` is formally smooth in the others
(Stacks 0329), and then passing to the limit.

Second, if `𝔪` is a finitely generated ideal then `R` is a quotient of a power series ring
`Λ[[x_1, …, x_n]]` in finitely many variables over a ring `Λ` which is either a field or a Cohen
ring: one sends `x_i` to a generator `y_i` of `𝔪` and the resulting map from the coefficient
ring's power series ring is surjective because it is surjective modulo `(x_1, …, x_n)` and both
sides are `(x_1, …, x_n)`-adically complete. Consequently every Noetherian complete local ring is
a quotient of a regular local ring.

## Main results

* `IsLocalRing.exists_isCoefficientRing_and_exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries`: a complete local
  ring has a coefficient ring, and if its maximal ideal is finitely generated it is a quotient of
  a power series ring in finitely many variables over a field or over a Cohen ring.

## Implementation notes

Completeness of `(R, 𝔪)` is `[IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R]`, which is exactly the source's
requirement that `R → lim_n R/𝔪ⁿ` be an isomorphism: `IsHausdorff` is its injectivity, that is
the source's `⋂ 𝔪ⁿ = 0`, and `IsPrecomplete` its surjectivity. No Noetherian hypothesis is
imposed, in keeping with the source, which imposes it nowhere in this theorem and asks for `𝔪`
finitely generated only in the second part.

"`R` is isomorphic to a quotient `Λ[[x_1, …, x_n]]/I`" is stated as the existence of a surjective
ring homomorphism `MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →+* R`. This is equivalent — the ideal `I` is the
kernel and the isomorphism is `RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective` — and it is the form the
source's own proof produces, so no choice of `I` or of the quotient presentation has to be made.
The `n` variables are indexed by `Fin n`, matching the source's `x_1, …, x_n`; `n = 0` occurs
exactly when `𝔪 = 0`.

The second part is stated for a field or a Cohen ring, not for a coefficient ring, because that is
what the source claims and it is the stronger statement: in the third case above the coefficient
ring is an Artinian local ring `Λ/pⁿΛ` for a Cohen ring `Λ`, and `R` is then presented over `Λ`
itself. As `IsCohenRing` is a class on a domain, `Λ` is quantified over together with anonymous
`CommRing` and `IsDomain` instance binders, which both disjuncts supply; `IsField Λ` rather than
`Field Λ` is the predicate form appropriate to a `Λ` carrying only a `CommRing` structure. The
`Λ` of the second part is a subring of `R` up to isomorphism in the first two cases and a Cohen
ring with residue field `R/𝔪` in the third, so it is asked for in the universe of `R`.

The source's two parts are the two conjuncts of a single statement, the second guarded by its own
hypothesis `(maximalIdeal R).FG` as an implication, so that the first part is not weakened by a
hypothesis the source does not give it.

Faithfulness. (1) Every hypothesis is used: `[IsLocalRing R]` provides both `𝔪` and the residue
field, `[IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R]` is what makes the limit of the lifted sections land
in `R` and what makes the power series map surjective, and `(maximalIdeal R).FG` is used only by
the second conjunct, whose antecedent it is — it is what bounds the number of variables, and the
first conjunct is stated without it, as in the source. (2) The scalars and base are the source's:
`Λ ⊆ R` is a subring of `R` itself, `𝔪` and the residue field are `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`
and `IsLocalRing.ResidueField R`, and the power series ring is taken over `Λ` with its map to `R`,
not over any localization or completion of it. (3) The source pins no map in either part: the
first conjunct asserts that a coefficient ring exists, all four of whose conditions are pinned by
`LocalSubring.IsCoefficientRing` (including the residue field map, which is the one induced by the
inclusion), and the second asserts that `R` is isomorphic to *some* quotient, so existence of a
surjection is the whole content. (4) Not degenerate: `R = ℤ_p` satisfies both hypotheses, its
coefficient ring is `Λ = ⊤` and its maximal ideal `pℤ_p` is generated by one element, so the
second conjunct presents it as `ℤ_p[[x]]/(x)`; `R = ℤ/p²ℤ` is a witness in which the coefficient
ring is Artinian and the `Λ` of the second conjunct is a Cohen ring, not a subring of `R`.

## References

* [StacksProject 032A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/032A), Theorem 10.160.8
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing
open Stacks.CompleteLocalRing.CohenStructure

/-- **Cohen structure theorem** (Stacks 032A). Let `(R, 𝔪)` be a complete local ring.
1. `R` has a coefficient ring: a local subring `Λ ⊆ R` which is complete with maximal ideal
   `Λ ∩ 𝔪`, whose residue field maps isomorphically onto that of `R`, and with `Λ ∩ 𝔪 = pΛ` for
   `p` the residue characteristic of `R`.
2. If `𝔪` is a finitely generated ideal, then `R` is isomorphic to a quotient
   `Λ[[x_1, …, x_n]]/I` where `Λ` is either a field or a Cohen ring; equivalently, there is a
   surjective ring homomorphism `Λ[[x_1, …, x_n]] → R`, whose kernel is `I`. -/
@[stacks 032A "Completeness of `R` is `IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R`, the source's \
  `R ≅ lim_n R/𝔪ⁿ`. The two parts are the two conjuncts, the second guarded by its own \
  hypothesis so that part (1) keeps the source's generality, and its `R ≅ Λ[[x_1, …, x_n]]/I` \
  is stated as the existence of a surjection `MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →+* R` with kernel `I`. \
  See the module docstring.", ega "0 19.8.8" "(i)"]
public theorem IsLocalRing.exists_isCoefficientRing_and_exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal R) R] :
    (∃ Λ : LocalSubring R, Λ.IsCoefficientRing) ∧
      ((maximalIdeal R).FG →
        ∃ (n : ℕ) (Λ : Type u) (_ : CommRing Λ) (_ : IsDomain Λ),
          (IsField Λ ∨ IsCohenRing Λ) ∧
            ∃ f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →+* R, Function.Surjective f) :=
  ⟨exists_isCoefficientRing_of_hasCoefficientRingHom R (hasCoefficientRingHom R),
    fun hFG => exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries_of_hasCoefficientRingHom R hFG
      (hasCoefficientRingHom R)⟩

end
